    "role": "client",
    "content": "I tried it out and it does what we agreed on. Pasting `example.com` fetched the real page title \"Example Domain\" automatically, and I could rename it and have the change stick. Saving with a note and tags worked, filtering by a tag showed the right link, searching found it by its note, and sorting put titles in the right order. When I pasted a link I'd already saved, it recognized it as an existing bookmark instead of duplicating. Deleting removed it cleanly, and the empty collection shows friendly guidance to paste a first link. The whole thing looks calm and easy to use.\n\nThis is what I wanted to save and manage my bookmarks. Accepted — nice work.",
